    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d934">

                <pb facs="1509" n="1481" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg1481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5611/5–454: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Mission at the
                        United Nations </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d934-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-05-04T20:15:00-04:00">May 4, 1954—8:15
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>539. Re Marshallese petition on Trust Territory of Pacific Islands (urtels 655
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">685</hi>] and 656 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >686</hi>]). Dept agrees special Security Council note should be avoided. In
                    Dept’s view <hi rendition="#italic">all</hi> petitions relating to TTPI fall
                    under para 3 of Security Council Resolution S/1280. In <pb facs="1510" n="1482"
                        xml:id="pg1482"/> no case in past so far as Dept aware has this para been
                    interpreted to require that SC be notified re petitions on TTPI in advance of
                    their consideration by Trusteeship Council. In past SC has been notified as to
                    petitions, like other TTPI matters, in annual TC report to SC. Dept sees no
                    reason for changing past practice and urges that SYG be asked follow it in this
                    case also.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d934-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d934-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Curtis C. Strong of the Office of Dependent Area Affairs (UND);
                    cleared with the Bureau of Far Eastern Affairs (FE), the Special Assistant to
                    the Secretary of State for Atomic Energy Matters (S/AE), and in draft with the
                    Department of the Interior; signed by the Director of the Office of Dependent
                    Area Affairs, O. Benjamin Gerig.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
